{"created": "2026-11-18T21:01:38.343054+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-20T21:00:29.156967+00:00", "id": 24353093, "conceptrecid": "22849807", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24353093", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22849807", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24353093", "metadata": {"title": "Recalculated woody crown hydraulic network properties and reduced principal component analyses of Caatinga and Cerrado trees", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24353093", "publication_date": "2026-11-18", "description": "<p><strong>Woody Crown Hydraulic Network (WCHN): corrected empirical crown networks, recalculated ecological analyses, and reproducible principal component analyses</strong></p>\n<p>This updated dataset version (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.24353093) contains 99 field woody crown hydraulic networks (WCHNs): 75 from the Cerrado and 24 from the Caatinga, including the documented reconstruction and correction of 20 existing Cerrado networks. The original source workbooks, six recalculated ecological comparison tables, corrected-topology audit workbook, and practical crown-reconstruction toolkit are preserved. The mathematical definitions, algebraic relationships, and derivations are maintained in a separate, independently citable Zenodo record (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.24181915).</p>\n<p><strong>New in this version</strong></p>\n<p>Reduced principal component analyses (PCAs) of five properties (NAV, revised VUL, LAT, BAS, and PTP) now incorporate the 20 corrected Cerrado WCHNs. The first two principal components explain 89.8% of variance in the 74 complete Cerrado WCHNs and 91.1% in the 24 Caatinga WCHNs.</p>\n<p>Network-size-adjusted analyses use ordinary least-squares regressions of ln(property) on ln(total node count, &Sigma;NO), followed by correlation-matrix PCAs of standardized residuals. The first two adjusted components account for 97.5% of residual standardized variance in Cerrado and 98.9% in Caatinga. Six pairwise partial correlations among NAV, BAS, PTP, and VUL are reported for each biome, together with Holm-adjusted significance tests.</p>\n<p>The deposit includes two explicit input CSV files, updated Excel workbooks, PCA figures, machine-readable JSON results, a reproducible Python analysis script, technical documentation, and a changelog. These materials enable independent reproduction and examination of the recalculated results.</p>\n<p><strong>Data provenance and interpretive limitations</strong></p>\n<p>The original Caatinga observations and the 55 Cerrado networks not redigitized in the correction exercise retain their previously stored numerical precision. One Cerrado WCHN with undefined BAS is excluded from the main PCA but remains documented in the input dataset and sensitivity analysis.</p>\n<p>The results characterize mathematical and topological relationships among WCHN properties. They do not independently demonstrate causal effects of crown topology on hydraulic safety or attainable tree height.</p>\n<p><strong>Citation and versioning</strong></p>\n<p>For analyses and files introduced in this update, cite the version-specific DOI: <strong>10.5281/zenodo.24353093</strong>.</p>\n<p>The concept DOI <strong>10.5281/zenodo.22849807</strong> identifies the complete version history of this dataset. The preceding published version is available at DOI <strong>10.5281/zenodo.24197048</strong>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Britto de Assis Prado, Carlos Henrique", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal de S\u00e3o Carlos", "orcid": "0000-0002-1652-2642"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Britto de Assis Prado, Carlos Henrique", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal de S\u00e3o Carlos", "type": "Researcher", "orcid": "0000-0002-1652-2642"}], "keywords": ["woody crown hydraulic network", "WCHN", "branching topology", "crown architecture", "hydraulic architecture", "plant hydraulics", "tree architecture", "network topology", "topological vulnerability", "navigability", "tree phenological groups", "Cerrado", "Caatinga", "hydraulic safety", "tree height", "computational plant modelling", "network reconstruction", "reproducible research"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2023.110345", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s11258-010-9797-7", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/j.jtbi.2020.110318", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s40626-024-00340-5", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21839645", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21852998", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.24082506", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "workflow", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.24181914", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "model", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.24220673", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "presentation", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "2.2.0", "references": ["Prado, C. H. B. A., & Trov\u00e3o, D. M. B. M. (2023). The woody crown network model incorporates maximum height. Ecological Modelling, 481, 110345. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2023.110345"], "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 5, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22849807"}}]}}, "title": "Recalculated woody crown hydraulic network properties and reduced principal component analyses of Caatinga and Cerrado trees", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records